From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:16:29 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] sidebar: archiving a thread with work running asks first
 instead of refusing

Operator ask of 2026-11-23, with 0166: archiving a thread that has
something running asks for a confirmation in a modal. Until now the sidebar
refused it -- upstream ignores the archive of a Running thread, 0029 refused
one with background tasks and 0072 one with a running subagent, with a toast
naming why -- and the row menu's Archive Thread did not ask at all.

Sidebar::confirm_archive_running_thread asks "Archive a thread that is still
working?", naming what runs (ARCHIVE_REFUSED_SUBAGENTS, ARCHIVE_REFUSED_TASKS,
or ARCHIVE_CONFIRM_TURN for the thread's own turn) and saying that work it
started in the background may keep running until the agent ends it -- the
archive stops the turn, through AgentPanel::cancel_thread, and nothing here
can promise more. "Archive" stops the turn and archives; "Keep It" leaves
both. Logged as sidebar event=archive_running_thread with the outcome.

Every way to archive goes through it: ArchiveSelectedThread (the refusal is
gone), the row menu's Archive Thread and the row's archive button, now
through archive_thread_or_ask, which asks only for a thread whose status is
Running, WaitingForConfirmation, Unconfirmed, Background or
WaitingForAnswer. The button is drawn again for a Background row, since the
action no longer refuses it.

Tests (sidebar_child_background_tests.rs, R4.3 revised): a running child
asks, "Keep It" keeps the row, "Archive" archives it; a waiting child and
background tasks ask; an idle thread archives without asking. Red: the three
asking tests fail without the change. sidebar suite green with 0166.
---

